Summary of the Invention
The present invention provides a system and method for a neuromorphic-orchestrated,
quantum-secured 6G communications network that overcomes the aforementioned
limitations of the prior art. The invention introduces a holistic, tri-layered architecture that
natively integrates an ultra-fast 6G Transport Layer, an ultra-secure Quantum Security Layer
(QSL), and an ultra-intelligent Neuromorphic Cognitive Orchestration Layer (NCOL).
The NCOL serves as the cognitive core of the network, implemented as a distributed system
of brain-inspired neuromorphic processors. Unlike conventional AI systems, the NCOL
operates on the principles of Spiking Neural Networks (SNNs), enabling event-driven,
asynchronous, and massively parallel processing. This results in decision-making and control
loops that operate at microsecond latencies with orders-of-magnitude lower power
consumption, providing the real-time intelligence necessary to manage the complexity of the
6G Transport Layer.
The QSL provides provable, long-term security against quantum adversaries through a hybrid
approach. It utilizes Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) for robust authentication and
control-plane security, while leveraging Quantum Key Distribution (QKD) over the assignee's
extensive fiber infrastructure to generate information-theoretically secure keys for encrypting
high-value user data.
A primary object of the invention is to solve the critical "trusted relay" vulnerability inherent in
prior art QKD networks. This is achieved through a novel method wherein the NCOL
continuously monitors the classical and quantum operational parameters of all QKD relays.
Using its real-time pattern recognition capabilities, the NCOL assigns a dynamic "Trust Score"
to each relay and intelligently routes quantum key generation requests along paths of highest
aggregate trust, effectively creating a self-healing security fabric that can preemptively
isolate potentially compromised nodes.
Another object of the invention is to introduce a new paradigm of network management,
termed Emergent Intent-Based Networking. High-level business or service intents are
translated into reward functions for the distributed SNNs of the NCOL. The network then
self-organizes its resources and configuration, allowing the optimal operational state to
emerge from the collective behavior of the neuromorphic agents, rather than being dictated
by rigid, pre-programmed policies. This enables unprecedented adaptability to novel
conditions and service requirements.
A further object of the invention is to provide a system for real-time predictive self-healing. By
processing high-dimensional data streams from the 6G layer's integrated sensing capabilities,
the NCOL's SNNs can detect subtle spatio-temporal precursors to hardware failures or
performance degradation, triggering proactive mitigation measures before any service impact
is experienced by the user.
Finally, an object of the invention is to introduce a Quantum-State-Aware Digital Twin. This is a
high-fidelity simulation of the entire network, managed by the NCOL, which models not only
the classical state of the transport layer but also the probabilistic quantum states of the QSL.
This allows the NCOL to perform "future shot" simulations to pre-validate complex
optimization and security strategies without risk to the live network, enabling a continuous
cycle of self-evolution and improvement. The invention provides a clear path to
commercialization through new premium service offerings, including
Quantum-Security-as-a-Service (QSaaS) and Neuromorphic-Orchestration-as-a-Service
(NOaaS).
